---
import ObfuscatedEmail from '../components/ObfuscatedEmail.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
---

<Layout title="Data privacy">
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="bg-grid absolute inset-0"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 text-center sm:px-6 sm:py-24">
      <h1 class="text-glow text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-5xl">Data privacy</h1>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-brand-gray">
        Privacy policy for the SmartMC website, mod, and companion app.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-24 sm:px-6">
    <div class="space-y-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-ink-900/60 p-6 text-sm text-brand-gray sm:p-10">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">1. Introduction</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          This privacy policy informs you about the nature, scope, and purpose of the processing of personal data
          within the SmartMC project, comprising this website (the "Website"), the SmartMC Minecraft server
          modification (the "Mod"), and the SmartMC companion mobile application (the "App"), collectively the
          "Services". It is addressed to visitors of the Website and to users of the Mod and the App.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">2. Controller</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The entity responsible for the processing of personal data described in this policy ("we", "us", "our")
          is Devsforge, as identified in the{' '}
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href={withBase('/imprint')}>Imprint</a>. For any
          question regarding this policy or the processing of your data, you may contact us using the details
          provided in Section 8 below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">3. The Website</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Website is served as a static site with no server-side application logic of its own. It does not set
          cookies, does not embed analytics, advertising, or tracking scripts of any kind, and does not maintain
          user accounts. Standard access logs (such as those generated automatically by our hosting or content
          delivery provider, typically containing an IP address, timestamp, requested resource, and user agent
          string) may be created purely for the operational purposes of security, abuse prevention, and diagnosing
          technical faults, and are outside our direct control as they are generated and retained by the underlying
          hosting infrastructure rather than by any code we operate.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Contributor names, usernames, and avatar images displayed on the Contributors page are retrieved from
          GitHub's public API at the time the Website is built and published, not in response to your visit. This
          data is limited to information that contributors have already made public through their GitHub profile
          and their public contributions to the project's source code repository.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">4. The Mod (processing on the server)</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Mod is designed to run entirely within the Minecraft server process on which it is installed. There is
          no Devsforge-operated backend, cloud service, or database that the Mod communicates with, and no data
          processed by the Mod is transmitted to us or to any other third party as part of its normal operation.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          When a player pairs the App with a server, the Mod stores, locally on that server and under the exclusive
          control of that server's operator, the player's Minecraft account identifier (UUID), an authentication
          token associated with the paired device, and the device and group records the player has configured. This
          data is retained for as long as the pairing remains active and is stored using the same mechanisms, and
          subject to the same operator control, as any other server-side modification's persistent data.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Because this data resides exclusively on the Minecraft server operated by a third party (the server
          owner), that server owner is the appropriate party to contact for access, correction, or deletion of data
          stored by the Mod on their server. We, as the developer of the Mod, do not have access to this data and
          cannot act on it directly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">5. The App</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The App establishes a direct, end-to-end encrypted connection to the Minecraft server you choose to pair
          it with, over the same network path used by the Minecraft client itself, as described in the{' '}
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href={withBase('/wiki/developers')}>developer
          documentation</a>. No intermediary server operated by us sits between the App and the Minecraft server, and
          no data exchanged over that connection is routed through, logged by, or made available to us.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The App stores, locally on your device, the cryptographic material and authentication token required to
          maintain your pairing with each server, together with locally cached, non-authoritative copies of device
          and group state for display purposes. This data remains on your device and is not synchronized to any
          service operated by us.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Push notifications are not part of the current version of the Services; alerts are delivered only while
          the App is open and actively connected to a paired server. Should push notification support be introduced
          in the future (see the{' '}
          <a class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" href={withBase('/roadmap')}>roadmap</a>), this
          policy will be updated in advance to describe the categories of data such a feature would require, the
          purpose of that processing, and the third-party push delivery providers involved, before the feature
          becomes active.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">6. Legal basis for processing</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the extent any processing described in this policy constitutes processing of personal data under
          applicable law (such as the EU General Data Protection Regulation), the legal basis relied upon is, as
          applicable: performance of a contract or steps taken at your request prior to entering into one
          (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR, in connecting your device to a server you have chosen to pair with), our legitimate interest in
          operating, securing, and maintaining the Services (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR), or your consent where explicitly
          given (Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">7. Your rights</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Subject to applicable law, you may have the right to request access to, correction of, deletion of, or
          restriction on the processing of your personal data, the right to data portability, and the right to
          object to processing carried out on the basis of legitimate interest. Where data is stored by a Mod
          instance under the control of a third-party server operator, these rights are exercised against that
          operator, typically by revoking your own pairing in-game or asking the operator to do so on your behalf.
          Where data is processed by us directly (for example, in connection with this Website or in response to a
          message you send us), you may exercise these rights by contacting us using the details in Section 8. You
          also have the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">8. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          For any question about this policy, to exercise a right described above with respect to data we process
          directly, or to report a suspected security or privacy issue, please contact us by email at{' '}
          <ObfuscatedEmail class="text-brand-teal underline hover:text-teal-300" />.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-white">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in the Services or in applicable law. The
          version published on this page is always the version currently in effect. We encourage you to review this
          page periodically.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
